  loss, and health care use during the peak and total influenza outbreak periods, and adverse events. RESULTS           
  Recipients of LAIV vaccine were as likely to experience 1 or more febrile illnesses as placebo recipients during      
  peak outbreak periods (13.2% for vaccine vs 14.6% for placebo; P=.19). However, vaccination significantly reduced     
