cardiovascular events (2.9% vs 4.7%; RR, 0.64 [95% CI, 0.48-0.86], P\u2009=\u2009.003) in published trials. A treatment 
interaction was detected between patients with (RR, 0.45 [95% CI, 0.32-0.63]) and without (RR, 0.94 [95% CI, 0.55-1.61])
recent ACS (P for interaction\u2009=\u2009.02). Results were similar with the addition of unpublished data. CONCLUSIONS 
AND RELEVANCE In a meta-analysis of RCTs, the use of influenza vaccine was associated with a lower risk of major adverse
